{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-convo/tests/proptests.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:58:31.532253Z","id":"34240bfa67f420ceff6a64f14e1fabee7c2da90187d4064575da4ae1754e96eb","body":{"detail":"The CHANGELOG says the point of the items stream is that deriving a growing Claude or Codex session is prefix-stable: a later derive starts with the same steps as an earlier one. proptests.rs checks three things: step ids are unique, derive -> extract -> derive is stable, and every turn of a chained stream is an ancestor of head. None of them derives a prefix of a view and compares it with the derive of the whole view. The turn() helper (lines 21-39) always sets group_id: None and token_usage: None, so the generated streams never reach the message-group accounting in derive_path (derive.rs:221-237). That code does break prefix stability, as a two-turn example shows (see the finding on derive.rs:221-237). The '#<n>' id-collision path also has no prefix check, although renamed ids are exactly where order-dependent state could go wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"8a8716b0f5a480f4b93ba867cc5a8298fadeef818038352ec69a9c2314667c7e"},"suggested_fix":"Add a proptest `derive_is_prefix_stable`: for a generated view and every k, assert that serde_json::to_value(derive(view.items[..k]).steps) equals the first steps of derive(view).steps. Give the generator an optional group_id drawn from a small pool and an optional token_usage so that group accounting is exercised.","summary":"The new proptest suite never tests prefix stability, the property this change exists for, and never generates group_id or token_usage","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-convo/tests/proptests.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:07:50.948697Z","id":"151061723131f93471073b83edc1cfab010c2dffae98e542af385c9a0fd7cfc2","body":{"detail":"The only properties are chained_turns_are_all_ancestors_of_head (line 216), derived_step_ids_are_unique (237) and derive_extract_derive_is_stable (247). The turn() helper (lines 21-39) hard-codes group_id: None and token_usage: None. A two-turn example shows derive.rs:221-231 breaks content prefix stability (see thread 7aafc5de), which this suite cannot catch. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"34240bfa67f420ceff6a64f14e1fabee7c2da90187d4064575da4ae1754e96eb","summary":"confirmed: proptests.rs has no prefix-stability property and never generates group_id or token_usage (new file in this change)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
